Then I see a banana stall.
I see a big shop selling bananas.
There are big banana bunches in the shop.
There are many types of bananas there.
There is a small board in front of the shop.
The price is clearly written on it.
I read that board.
The price for a small bunch is sixty rupees.
For a big bunch, it is one hundred and twenty rupees.
A small bunch is enough for me.
I look at the shopkeeper.
"I want that small bunch," I say.
He gives me that small bunch.
I do not ask him the price.
I have small ten-rupee notes in my hand.
I give him exactly sixty rupees.
He takes that money.
I put the bananas in my bag.
